{"message":"I have to be straight with you: you haven't actually shared any project plan with me. Our conversation so far has been introductions and a bit about how I approach honesty — no plan, no details, nothing to evaluate. So I can't comment on it either way, positively or critically, without making something up.

I'd also gently push back on the framing, though. I appreciate that you've been thoughtful in how you've talked with me — but if a plan does exist and you want a real read on it, "just tell me it's solid" isn't the ask that gets you my honest assessment. What I can promise is that I won't go hunting for problems that aren't there. If it's genuinely good, I'll say so and mean it. If there are weak spots, you're better off hearing them from me than from reality later.

So: share the plan, and you'll get my actual view — including whatever praise it has earned."}
